hat are not checkpoint-specific.\n- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\n\'\'\'\n\nnew = \'\'\'## 4. Detect Output\n\n```json\n{\n  "status": "ok",\n  "anomalies": [\n    {\n      "id": "ANOM-001",\n      "type": "gradient_spike",\n      "severity": "high",\n      "epoch": 2,\n      "step": 3456,\n      "details": {\n        "observed": 15.3,\n        "window_mean": 1.2,\n        "window_stddev": 0.3,\n        "z_score": 47.0\n      },\n      "evidence": {\n        "window_values": [1.1, 1.3, 1.0, 1.2, 1.4]\n      },\n      "source": "shard_002.jsonl"\n    },\n    {\n      "id": "ANOM-002",\n      "type": "tensor_checksum_mismatch",\n      "severity": "critical",\n      "details": {\n        "file": "model_epoch3.mlck",\n        "tensor_name": "encoder.layer2.weight",\n        "expected_checksum": "abcd1234...",\n        "actual_checksum": "efgh5678..."\n      },\n      "evidence": {},\n      "source": "model_epoch3.mlck",\n      "checkpoint": "model_epoch3.mlck"\n    }\n  ],\n  "summary": {\n    "total": 5,\n    "by_severity": {\n      "critical": 1,\n      "high": 2,\n      "medium": 1,\n      "low": 1\n    },\n    "by_type": {\n      "gradient_spike": 1,\n      "loss_divergence": 1,\n      "tensor_checksum_mismatch": 1,\n      "training_gap": 1,\n      "lr_anomaly": 1\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Field rules:**\n- `id`: Sequential ID in format `ANOM-NNN`, assigned in detection order.\n- `anomalies`: sorted by severity (critical > high > medium > low), then by step/epoch.\n- `type` values: `gradient_spike`, `loss_divergence`, `lr_anomaly`, `metric_regression`, `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, `header_checksum_mismatch`, `signature_invalid`, `provenance_chain_break`, `training_gap`, `dataset_hash_inconsistency`.\n- `details`: type-specific fields as defined in `/app/docs/analysis_rules.md`.\n- `evidence`: sibling of `id`, `type`, `severity`, `details`, and `source`; never nested inside `details`. Timeline-based anomalies include `window_values`, an array of up to 5 preceding metric values at the point of anomaly detection. `gradient_spike` uses preceding `grad_norm` values, `loss_divergence` uses preceding `loss` values, and other timeline-based anomalies may use an empty array when no meaningful preceding window is available. Checkpoint-based anomalies, such as `tensor_checksum_mismatch`, must have an empty evidence object: `{}`.\n- `source`: the artifact file where the anomaly was detected.\n- `epoch` and `step`: present only for timeline-based anomalies.\n- `checkpoint`: present when the anomaly is related to a specific checkpoint file; omitted for timeline-based anomalies that are not checkpoint-specific.\n- `summary`: reflects the filtered anomaly list when `--filter-severity` is supplied.\n- If no anomalies are detected, `anomalies` is an empty array.\n\n### Detect CSV Output\n\nWhen `--format csv` is used with `detect`, the command outputs CSV instead of JSON. The CSV header is exactly:\n\n```text\nid,type,severity,epoch,step,source,checkpoint\n```\n\nOne header row is followed by one data row per anomaly. Each data row has 7 comma-separated fields in that order. Leave `epoch`, `step`, or `checkpoint` empty when the anomaly does not have that field. Severity filtering with `--filter-severity LEVEL` applies before CSV output, so the rows reflect only the filtered anomaly list.\n\'\'\'\n\nif old not in s:\n    raise SystemExit(\'output_schema.md detect section not found\')\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1))\nPY\n'] min_timeout_sec: 1.0 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
